in recent days demonstrators have taken  to the streets across China to voice  frustration with their government's  strict zero coveted policy these  protests have become one of the greatest  public shows of defiance against the  Chinese Communist party in decades so  what exactly is zero covet and why is  Chinese leadership insisting on it zero  covid or dynamic zero copied centers  around eradicating the virus completely  rather than living with it the Communist  Regime uses strict lockdowns isolation  and mass testing in areas where cases  have been reported the approach is so  strict that entire cities housing  millions of people have been locked down  over just a few covet cases with reports  of Shoppers and workers fleeing stores  and factories to avoid being locked  inside there have also been instances  where citizens struggle to get food  Medical Care and other Essentials as  well as being prevented from leaving  buildings during earthquakes and other  disasters  one particular incident which sparked  this recent surge of unrest was an  apartment fire in arumchi the capital of  the xinjiang region in China's Northwest  10 people died in the fire and many  believe lockdowns prevented people from  escaping and help from arriving but  authorities deny lockdowns were a factor  in the deaths these protests are not the  first against the Chinese government's  coveted strategy but they do represent a  particular challenge for president Xi  Jinping demonstrators have openly  criticized him for the policy and some  have even called for him to step down  but the president has continued to  defend the approach stating China has  not suffered the same death rates as  other countries  the country's official figures have been  questioned for their accuracy but there  have been 5 200 reported kova deaths in  China since the pandemic started with a  population of over 1.4 billion people  this would make it one of the lowest  coveted death rates per capita in the  world at this stage it is unclear how  China moves forward from zero covid  without major difficulties  the country has poor vaccination rates  and the shots available to Chinese  citizens are not as effective as the  MRNA vaccines available in other  countries on top of this in the three  years that China has pursued zero covet  it is not vaccinated its most vulnerable  people nor has it improved the Health  Care system to cope with outbreaks UK  Health analytics firm airfinity predicts  as many as 2.1 million people could die  if the policy is lifted and believes  improving vaccination rates among its  elderly will be key before reopening but  given recent uproar there are signs that  the CCP is reconsidering its strategy on  November 30th Vice Premier Sun Chen Lan  who heads the country's pandemic  response told the National Health  commission they were facing a new  situation as they tackle a virus with  weakening pathogenicity according to  Reuters officials in Guangzhou have  begun to lift lockdowns in parts of the  city just a day after protests that  involve clashes with Riot police another  shift in strategy involves allowing  people with asymptomatic infections and  people who have been in close contact  with infected visuals to quarantine at  home rather than at a government center  officials made no mention of the ongoing  protests against zero covet however it  appears likely they served as a catalyst  for the changes
 

